WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:20.370
This is the truth that Odin hid from us.
We've coined it "Norse mythology."

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.370
The end of the world foreseen
by god has already happened?

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.250
This doesn't change the fact
that Odin remains our ally.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:36.290
At this point, I think we should be
questioning whether he truly is or not.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.080
We're revisiting that all over again?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.200
An enemy of unknown origin
and god-granted means to fight back...

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.200
We had nations secretly investigating
Odin's identity. What do we know?

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.410
The heck--?

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.700
"The heck" is quite the greeting, humans.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.410
That voice is...

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.330
God.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.910
A second meeting. A second coming.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.370
God Odin! Explain yourself!

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.250
Before, I gave you the power to fight.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.410
Therefore, I now give you motive to fight.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.250
That's Mt. Fuji Pillar...

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.120
Go figure.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.660
The Pillars are sided with Odin?!

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.250
You were recently shown
the power of my friend, Thor.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:38.870
Many perished that day.
But no, not nearly enough!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:43.200
I gave you the power to fight.
I gave you motive to fight.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.790
And... I gave you enemies to fight.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.870
Odin!

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.290
Resist your destruction, humans!

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.290
I'll say it again.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:56.000
The great battle is near.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.700
The coming of Ragnarök is nigh.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.830
"Episode 10: The Eve Before
the Battle of Tateyama Bay!"

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.830
Ahhhh! Feels so good!

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.910
You've been working hard.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.370
Hmm... I think it's Azu, Claudy,
and all the others who have been.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:48.410
They've been so busy after
learning about the mural and gods.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:54.160
I don't want 'em to wear themselves out,
but you know how Azu is.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.250
If she gets bad,
I'm sure Clo will make her stop.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.660
Well, I know, but...

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.450
You'd rather be at her side while you worry?

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:09.500
Hmm? You seem stronger now, Sono.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.040
Well, I am the youngest Named candidate!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.250
Hey, Miko!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.910
I couldn't help it!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.200
What's wrong?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:28.870
Now that we're back in Tateyama,
it's back to the same old routine for me.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.290
I feel like I should be doing something.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.330
The civilians came back too, right?

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.660
Yeah. Everyone loves their hometown.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.750
Still, it seems so quiet.
It's not like Tateyama at all.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.370
Any other year,
we'd be preparing for the festival.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.870
Festival?

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:53.120
The annual summer festival.
But it's not likely--

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.330
--That's it!
--Miko?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.790
Let's have the summer festival!

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.200
After Odin's declaration of war,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.450
nations have been working together to analyze
the data our scouts retrieved from Valhalla.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:12.700
We've identified the Fuji Pillar giant
named Thor and various other gods.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.540
Týr, Freyja, Heimdallr...
Plus Loki, and many more.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.410
And? What do the experts say?

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:27.620
The Pillars are sided with Odin,
and somehow, Norse mythology was lost.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.950
Ragnarök is already over, huh?

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:37.040
I told you I was right.
Not that I'm happy about it.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.580
Agreed. How are other nations reacting?

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:46.080
The response has been largely united.
After all, he declared war at a summit meeting.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.000
It was a slap in the face
to humanity as a whole.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.660
How's our readiness?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:56.000
Hyakuri and other bases
are racing to get back on their feet.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.450
They'll be good to go in two weeks.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:01.330
Good to go. In other words...

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:04.200
Ready to reattack Fuji Pillar.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.660
The last battle beat up the enemy too.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:13.160
They haven't recovered just yet.
Fighting is a gamble for both sides.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.910
And that's putting it nicely.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.370
Azuzu, you okay?

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:20.500
We can't throw in the towel just yet!

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:26.290
The info we brought back got the
world moving. We can't just sit around.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:31.250
Since the declaration of war,
Pillars have been appearing sporadically.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:37.120
However, the power of the
Valkyries hasn't been taken away.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.040
Strange, isn't it?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:45.250
Odin's behind it all, yet leaves his protection?
Gods boggle my mind.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.750
But without Odin,
there won't be any new Valkyries.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:54.200
Valkyries receive Odin's blessing
and are bestowed wings.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:58.000
In other words,
if the wings we have now are lost...

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.660
Humanity is done for.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.660
I'll keep analyzing the data
from the last battle.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.500
Because... that's my job.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:23.370
Guess my job is getting support
from the big wigs. Good grief.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:28.370
Claudia, can you join me?
Your presence can be persuasive.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:31.120
Roger. But Azuzu--

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.700
Don't worry.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:38.160
I'm gonna work on our strategy
till the last minute to help our odds out.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.450
Azuzu, don't push yourself.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:44.450
You're the one who said
the world's depending on me.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.410
Now's one of those times.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.870
Understood.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:55.200
Azuzu, give it your best.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.700
I always give my best.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.830
You got let out awfully quick.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:18.120
Of course I did. It's not like I'm sick.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:22.580
Other than here, my body's just fine.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:26.080
--Can you fly?
--At this point, who knows?

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:31.700
It doesn't feel much different
on the ground, but I guess we'll see.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.830
Come to say I should retire?

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.540
That choice is always out there.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:45.250
You know, Lily always put other people first.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:50.620
I told her it's fine to be more selfish,
but that's just who she was.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:57.000
And Ortlinde... Sakura always made
sure everyone got home from battle.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.000
That's why she was always the last to land.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.120
I'm not retiring.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:09.370
At first, I was reluctant to fly,
but now, I yearn for the sky.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:14.620
I'm not the type to sit around
and pray while you guys are in the air.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.500
Are you upset?

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.580
No. That's reassuring, my comrade.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:27.410
See you in the sky. May the wings guide you.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:31.330
Yeah. May they guide you and your comrades.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.950
I should head home to Tateyama.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:49.950
Tateyama is home to me, huh?

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:55.910
Azu! Time to wake up!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:01.700
Sheesh! You even made a mess on your bed!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.830
You're sure working hard to help everyone.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.500
Of course I am.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.870
Why haven't you been cleaning?
You abandoned me.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:15.750
Sorry, sorry! I've been busy
with stuff, so don't pout!

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.500
I'm not pouting!

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.370
What's that?

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:25.080
I'm glad you asked! It just came in today!

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.910
Mm-hmm! Just like I thought!
You look good in black!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.950
I look good in everything.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.870
Yeah, but especially!

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.910
Isn't that a yukata? What's it for?

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:40.200
They're a must-have for summer festivals!

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.000
I've got my own too!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.750
Hold on just a sec. What summer festival?

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.830
Tateyama's summer festival.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:53.540
It's usually tomorrow and it almost
got canceled, so I've been busy.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:56.870
--It's been super hectic!
--Festival?

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.410
Azu, your button.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:04.450
A festival during <i>this </i>crisis?
How'd that strike you as a good idea?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:09.200
This is no time for a festival!
No one wants it but you!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.160
Everyone's helping out, though.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:19.660
Sono, the city people, the base crew...
They all wanna make it happen.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.910
Unbelievable...

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:28.120
Azu, I know it's been hard on you.
I get it. So, let's...

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.450
You think you know how I feel?

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.700
You have no idea!

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.620
Azu!

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.580
Why am I surrounded by such idiots?!

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.370
Sigu...

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.870
...ruri!

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.000
Sigu...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.500
...ruri!

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:47.330
"Pilot Blondie (Age 28)"
"Pilot Shades (Age 27)"        "Pilot Shaggy (Age 29)"

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:54.000
"Pilot Blondie (Age 28)"
"Pilot Shades (Age 27)"        "Pilot Shaggy (Age 29)"

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:54.000
Huh? Azu? She was
hustling towards the cafeteria.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.870
"Pilot Blondie (Age 28)"
"Pilot Shades (Age 27)"        "Pilot Shaggy (Age 29)"

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.870
But she zoomed past us.

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.830
"Rookie Valkyrie Kurumi Suzuhara (Age 14)"
"Rookie Valkyrie Moe Isurugi (Age 14)"

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:58.830
Azu? You mean Komagome?

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:03.950
"Rookie Valkyrie Kurumi Suzuhara (Age 14)"
"Rookie Valkyrie Moe Isurugi (Age 14)"

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:03.950
She went flying out the back door
and slammed her knee real good.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:09.950
"Maintenance Team Leader (Age 55)"

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:09.950
That crybaby completely ran by and ignored me.
Next time, I'll chew her out!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.330
"Maintenance Team Leader (Age 55)"

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.330
Uh, she went running around
the building... Careful with that!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:19.500
Azu? Uh, haven't seen her.
I'll let you know if I do.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:24.950
Okay, please do!
Well, I'm gonna check over this way!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:28.120
Miko left.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:32.000
Dammit! Why is everyone tattling on me?

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.790
'Cuz of how you treat them?

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.040
I did nothing wrong!

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.040
You hear about the festival?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:44.000
Yeah, I'm preparing for it.
Festivals need flowers, especially tomorrow's.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:50.580
It's understandable you're upset.
We're in a crisis, after all.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:56.330
But everyone's helping willingly.
I'm sure they want something out of it.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.830
What do you mean, "something"?

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:02.160
Like to make memories... or to look back.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:10.910
Do you think it's weird that
all I remember is Yayoi's smile?

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:15.500
Not really. Amatsuka's someone who smiled a lot.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:21.450
Yeah. I hope when people
remember me, I'm smiling too.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.040
Don't be a memory just yet.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:28.250
Yeah, I know.
But I wanna be in lots of memories.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:33.120
I won't let a mean god make me sad
and ruin all the photos of me.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:36.160
It seems like you're stronger now.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.000
Miko said that too.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.830
Maybe you guys are, but I...

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.200
Thanks for letting me hide. Later.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:53.750
Azu... When I make memories and look back,
I'd like to do it with everyone.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:00.120
Miyako!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:04.500
Oh, Claudy! You're back early!

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.620
I kinda missed you guys.
The civilians told me what's going on.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.870
Is that a yukata for the festival?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.870
Claudy, do you think it's stupid of me?

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:20.290
You're doing it for a reason, right?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.870
Azu got mad at me though.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.830
And you're trying to patch things up?

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.290
Before that, I've gotta find where she went.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:32.700
You met all the big wigs, huh? How'd it go?

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:38.790
Everyone seems pretty hopeful.
They all promised their full support.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.040
We can't lose.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.160
We won't lose. Azu's planning it.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.700
You sure trust her, don't you?

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.830
Azu will steer us right!

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:54.120
She always makes the right smart-person choice,
so I make the dumb-person choice!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.950
When we're together, we can never be wrong!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:03.160
Oh dear! Is that right?

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:07.660
--That's right!
--Azuzu would've loved to hear that.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.870
What a shame.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:12.660
I bet. Where in the world could she be?

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:19.450
Sorry, Claudy. I've gotta go see Azu.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:25.450
Yeah, be careful. Sometimes
she trips when nothing's there.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:32.250
I got a yukata for you too!
One that compliments your pretty, blonde hair!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:43.450
When we were recruits, you used
to stare at the sea from high above.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.910
All day, I think...

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:56.790
Just how many lives did we change
with the info we brought back?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:01.750
I'm a genius. I'm smart and cute, so I know...

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:07.660
If our next attack fails,
humanity is done for. We lose.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:10.250
I've been thinking how to avoid that.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:14.500
Strategies to win,
formations, using our Valkyries...

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:19.000
On... and on... and on...

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:23.660
You're such a crybaby, Azu.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.040
Sorry I'm a weakling.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:31.120
You might be a crybaby,
but I never said you're a weakling.

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.330
I'm scared.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.750
I'm scared too. We're even.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.450
It's a weight I can't shoulder.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.500
Then I'll carry half.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.790
We might die next time.

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:48.370
Maybe.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.250
But if you die, I'll be dead too.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.330
I'll wake you in heaven for breakfast.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.250
No thanks. Your voice is too loud.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:02.580
If you wake me nicely, I'll think about it.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.000
Only if you wear clothes to bed for once.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.370
What?!

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.450
"Southernmost Point, Bousou Peninsula"

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.750
"Southernmost Point, Bousou Peninsula"

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.750
There, all done!

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.750
About the festival...

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.660
Yup! We're meeting at the sea!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:17.950
The sea...

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:20.950
Azu, will you join us?

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:23.660
Under one condition.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.830
You've gotta help me put it on.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.580
"Bousou Festival"

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.620
Hey!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.750
Ooh! You two managed to put yours on!

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.120
Clo knows a lot about yukatas!
I'm impressed!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.160
You can thank my father for that.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.500
--What?
--Oh, nothing!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.200
Your yukata's cute. Is Azu's special?

00:17:56.200 --> 00:18:01.410
Yup! Azu's is special!
I fixed it up with all my heart!

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.000
Snuggle snuggle!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.500
Well, shall we?

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.500
Should we head to the beach?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:35.870
You and Sono can. Azu and I have other plans.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:37.580
Hold onto these!

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:40.540
Hey, what's the deal? I never--

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:41.950
It's fine, it's fine!

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:44.910
No, it's not! Careful, idiot!

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.910
Well, I guess we're this way. Let's go.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.250
You're late, ponytail!

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.290
Sorry! Is it ready?

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:54.250
Yup!

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.500
Now we're talking!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:00.410
C'mon! Azu, hop in!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.750
Wha--?! It's way too cramped!

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:08.580
If you squeeze in and we squeeze together,
it'll be fine! C'mon, Azu!

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:19.410
Water lanterns... To guide the dead, huh?

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:25.120
It's equally meant to console the living.
That's why it's important.

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:27.330
Where are Miyako and Azuzu?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.750
You'll know soon enough. Hear that?

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.750
Lanterns in the sea and wings in the sky.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:49.370
What a show. That's Miyako for you.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:54.580
Yeah. It's so Miko, but it's so Tateyama too.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:58.790
'Cuz there's a lot of people
we couldn't send off.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:19:59.250
